    {
      "v": 6,
      "zh": "当时亚兰王利汛收回以拉他归与亚兰，将犹大人从以拉他赶出去。亚兰人（有译以东人的）就来到以拉他，住在那里，直到今日。",
      "en": "(At that time King Rezin of Syria[NOTE:1] recovered Elat for Syria; he drove the Judahites from there.[NOTE:2] Syrians[NOTE:3] arrived in Elat and live there to this very day.)",
      "notes": [
        "Some prefer to read “the king of Edom” and “for Edom” here. The names Syria (Heb “Aram,” אֲרָם, ʾaram) and Edom (אֱדֹם, ʾedom) are easily confused in the Hebrew consonantal script.",
        "Heb “from Elat.”",
        "The consonantal text (Kethib), supported by many medieval Hebrew mss, the Syriac version, and some mss of the Targum and Vulgate, read “Syrians” (Heb “Arameans”). The marginal reading (Qere), supported by the LXX, Targums, and Vulgate, reads “Edomites.”"
      ],
